{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1kRa8HphSQjZCuTN4d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: build it, but ship it as a randomized rollout with a holdout. Don't do more research first.**\n\n**Why build**\n- The evidence is strong. This was a randomized test with a behavioral outcome from pharmacy records, not self-report. A 13-point drop (31% to 18%) on roughly 400 per arm has a 95% interval of about 7 to 19 points. That assumes an even split, so check the actual arm sizes.\n- The control arm's 31% matches the pharmacy-wide baseline. So email opt-in patients don't look unusually prompt or late, which is reassuring.\n- The cost is small and reversible: three weeks for two engineers.\n\n**What the email result doesn't tell you**\n- Email opt-in patients chose that channel. Push users may respond differently, so expect the effect to differ, possibly smaller.\n- Push has its own failure modes: patients who have notifications off, who never open the app, or who ignore the alert. Coverage may matter more than the effect per recipient.\n- The test showed that a reminder works. It didn't show which part matters (timing, wording, or the channel itself).\n\n**How to run it**\n1. Randomize eligible app users, with a holdout of roughly 20–50%, so the build also measures push's effect.\n2. Use the same primary metric: collected more than seven days late.\n3. Track push permission rate and delivery or open rate as diagnostics.\n4. Treat push as an addition to email, not a replacement. Check whether patients who get both do better.\n5. Decide in advance what result would make you stop or change course, such as an effect under 3 points.\n\nExtra research would mostly repeat what the holdout will tell you, and it would cost time."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3455,"cache_read_input_tokens":5027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3455},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dc7d41c-8829-4e0c-b834-4bcfce3db6a8","uuid":"5862eb95-9d1f-4cc0-b6dd-c50d72896706","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:16:18.487Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1kRJkjn8KNVRnqJMSD"}
